Firstly, regarding EU-only hosting, our standard data residency policy already specifies that all data is stored within the EU, which aligns with this requirement. Additionally, our cross-border transfer policy prohibits data transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis, ensuring we do not transfer any sensitive information outside of the European Union.

For encryption and protection of sensitive data, we can utilize anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to ensure that personal data is handled appropriately. This aligns with our capability to implement data anonymisation before any model update or processing.

To ensure explainability of AI recommendations post-hoc, our AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. These measures can contribute to providing transparent and understandable AI-driven outputs, although we must conduct further analysis to fully satisfy the client's specific requirements for explainability.

Regarding the prohibition on automated decisions without explicit agent validation, our decision automation constraint explicitly states that no decision can be automated without an agent's explicit validation. This aligns with the client's requirement, ensuring that agents remain in control of all decision-making processes assisted by AI.

Lastly, to further reinforce GDPR compliance, we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and reachable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it, which ensures that there is a dedicated point of contact for data protection matters. Our company also has experience with regulatory frameworks including the GDPR, as indicated by our experience with RGPD/GDPR and other relevant EU regulations.

By implementing these measures, we can ensure that our solution meets the client's strict GDPR compliance requirements while providing explainable AI recommendations and ensuring that agents have explicit control over decision-making processes.
